title: December 2024

@left_nomination_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Three credible nominees arrive with offices, constituencies and incompatible theories of power; every nomination method visibly redistributes ownership of the campaign.
title: Choose the Left's presidential candidate
subtitle: Biejat, Dziemianowicz-Bąk or a common mandate for Zandberg
face-image: img/poland/events/wlodzimierz-czarzasty-2019.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 20
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 12
on-arrival: {!
const razemFederated =
    String(Q.left_merger_structure || "") == "federation" &&
    Q.merger_razem_present &&
    String(Q.razem_org_status || "") != "departed";
const razemOutside =
    Q.razem_split || Q.razem_party_formed || !Q.razem_in_left;
const razemCampaignStrength = razemOutside
    ? Math.max(
        Number(Q.razem_exit_strength) || 0,
        Number(Q.razem_vote_intent) || 0
    )
    : Number(Q.razem_strength) || 0;
const razemCohesive =
    Q.razem_cooperation_protocol || Q.razem_breakaway_protected ||
    (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) >= 55;
const razemRupture = (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) >= 45;
Q.pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible =
    !razemFederated && !razemCohesive && razemRupture &&
    razemCampaignStrength >= 8 ? 1 : 0;
Q.news_headline = "The Left opens its 2025 presidential nomination";
!}

= December 2024 — Who carries the Left into the presidential election?

New Left co-chairs **Włodzimierz Czarzasty** and **Robert Biedroń** bring three
routes to the national council. **Magdalena Biejat**, deputy marshal of the
Senate, offers housing, care and a bridge to Razem's political generation.
<span class="party-lewica"><b>Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk</b></span>, [? if left_in_government: our labour minister?]
[? if not left_in_government: former labour minister and Sejm deputy?], offers
a workers-and-public-services campaign tied to a record of delivery. **Adrian
Zandberg**, Razem's co-founder and leading parliamentary voice, offers the
clearest economic opposition to both the right and liberal coalition policy.

[? if razem_split = 1: October produced two organisations with competing
accounts of responsibility: Biejat's cooperative current stayed beside New
Left while Zandberg took Razem into opposition. Two presidential candidates
would turn that argument into a national count.?] [? if razem_split = 0: The
October agreement kept the common camp intact, but separate presidential
nominations could reopen the rupture it postponed.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: Biejat or Dziemianowicz-Bąk would carry the gains
and compromises of Lewica's time in office. Zandberg can ask which of them were
worth entering government for.?] [? if left_in_government = 0: No nominee can
campaign on current ministerial delivery. The contest is instead over which
kind of opposition can return the Left to power.?]

[? if pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Choosing Biejat or
Dziemianowicz-Bąk gives New Left its own voice and leaves a sufficiently
separate, organised Razem free to register Zandberg. A primary asks members to
close the split for one campaign. Handing Zandberg a negotiated mandate
produces one candidate, but asks New Left's own apparatus to surrender the
nomination.?]

[? if not pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Razem has neither the
organisational rupture nor the independent strength for a second committee.
Federation, a binding cooperation protocol or simple weakness therefore turns
a Biejat or Dziemianowicz-Bąk nomination into the common Left campaign. A
primary or a negotiated Zandberg mandate can still decide who leads it.?]

- @biejat_confirm
- @dziemianowicz_bak_nomination
- @biejat_primary
- @biejat_zandberg

@biejat_confirm
title: [? if pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Confirm Biejat and let Razem run separately?][? if not pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Confirm Biejat as the common Left nominee?]
subtitle: [? if pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Give the cooperative Left and Zandberg's opposition separate ballots on their strategy.?][? if not pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Razem remains inside the common campaign because no credible rupture supports a second committee.?]
on-arrival: {!
const separate = Boolean(Q.pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible);
Q.pres_2025_left_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat";
Q.pres_2025_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat";
Q.pres_2025_razem_candidate = separate ? "Adrian Zandberg" : "None";
Q.pres_2025_united_left = separate ? 0 : 1;
Q.pres_2025_nomination_method = separate
    ? "Separate candidacies" : "Common Left nomination";
Q.pres_2025_unity_effect = separate ? 0 : 0.6;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_strength += separate ? 1 : 3;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 2;
Q.razem_cooperation += separate ? -3 : 2;
Q.party_unity += separate ? 0 : 2;
Q.news_headline = separate
    ? "Two Left candidacies prepare to measure government and opposition"
    : "Biejat receives the common Left presidential nomination";
!}

[? if pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Biejat accepts New Left's nomination
and begins building a campaign around care, housing and the practical use of
institutions. Zandberg answers with a Razem candidacy centred on wages, public
investment and the price of compromise. Their programmes overlap more than
either campaign's account of power.?]

[? if pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Journalists now have a simple nightly
question—why should a voter choose one Left candidate over the other? The two
organisations gain clean identities and lose the shelter of a common result.
The first-round count will be read as a verdict on the split itself.?]

[? if not pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Razem accepts Biejat's nomination
inside the common campaign. Its organisers keep their programme and internal
voice, but federation, cooperation and the balance of forces leave no honest
case for pretending that a second national committee already exists.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Put both nomination papers on the events desk

@dziemianowicz_bak_nomination
title: Nominate Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk
subtitle: [? if pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Run on work and public services while an organised Razem fields Zandberg.?][? if not pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Run a common Left campaign on work and public services.?]
