    ? "Dziemianowicz-Bąk carries New Left's presidential campaign"
    : "Dziemianowicz-Bąk carries the common Left presidential campaign";
!}

Dziemianowicz-Bąk accepts a nomination built around wages, labour inspection,
schools and the public services that make freedom usable. [? if
left_in_government: She can name measures Lewica delivered from office, but
every coalition retreat is now part of her record.?][? if not
left_in_government: She turns her ministerial record into an argument for a
Left capable of returning to office without abandoning its programme.?]

[? if pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Razem registers Zandberg separately.
The two campaigns will often diagnose the same economic failures; voters will
judge whether implementation or the freedom to oppose offers the more
credible remedy.?]

[? if not pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible: Razem supplies organisers and a
sharper economic brief to the same campaign. Dziemianowicz-Bąk carries the
nomination; Zandberg retains the right to test its labour and investment
programme without inventing a rival ballot line.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Put both nomination papers on the events desk

@biejat_primary
title: Reopen the decision through a Left-wide primary
subtitle: Spend 2 resources and let members choose which figure carries a common programme.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: There is no time or money for a credible primary.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.pres_2025_primary_roll =
    this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const zandbergScore =
    (Number(Q.razem_strength) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) * 0.25 +
    (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) * 0.15 +
    Q.pres_2025_primary_roll * 15;
const biejatScore =
    (Number(Q.progressives_strength) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.spring_strength) || 0) * 0.45 +
    (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) * 0.20 +
    (1 - Q.pres_2025_primary_roll) * 15;
Q.pres_2025_left_candidate =
    zandbergScore > biejatScore ? "Adrian Zandberg" : "Magdalena Biejat";
Q.pres_2025_candidate = Q.pres_2025_left_candidate;
Q.pres_2025_razem_candidate = "None";
Q.pres_2025_united_left = 1;
Q.pres_2025_nomination_method = "Open Left-wide primary";
Q.pres_2025_unity_effect = 1.1;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_strength += 5;
Q.party_unity += 4;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.pres_2025_left_candidate + " wins an open Left primary";
!}

Party halls and union rooms fill for a contest the leadership can no longer
settle by arithmetic in Warsaw. Biejat argues that cooperation can turn a
programme into law; Zandberg argues that a programme without the power to say
no becomes decoration.

[? if pres_2025_left_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat": Biejat wins the common
nomination. Zandberg concedes before his organisers and keeps Razem inside the
campaign, giving her a mandate broader than New Left's original announcement.?]
[? if pres_2025_left_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg": Zandberg wins the common
nomination. Biejat withdraws and asks her cooperative current to honour the
ballot, giving his programme access to an apparatus that had not intended to
serve it.?]

One name reaches the ballot and the primary supplies photographs of a reunited
Left. It does not erase the argument over government; it binds both sides to
fight that argument after the presidential campaign rather than through it.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the primary mandate on the events desk

@biejat_zandberg
title: Offer Zandberg the common nomination and a programme mandate
subtitle: Use accumulated trust to buy one candidacy; ask New Left's apparatus to surrender its choice.
choose-if: razem_cooperation >= 48
unavailable-subtitle: Razem sees a takeover attempt rather than a common candidacy.
on-arrival: pres_2025_left_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg"; pres_2025_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg"; pres_2025_razem_candidate = "None"; pres_2025_united_left = 1; pres_2025_nomination_method = "Negotiated programme mandate"; pres_2025_unity_effect = 0.4; pres_2025_campaign_strength += 6; razem_dissent -= 8; razem_cooperation += 6; barons_dissent += 8; spring_dissent += 5; labor_credibility += 3; news_headline = "Zandberg receives a common Left mandate"

Czarzasty and Biedroń withdraw Biejat's nomination and offer Zandberg a
written mandate on housing, wages and public investment. He accepts because
the preceding cooperation makes the offer credible, not because the split has
been declared imaginary. Biejat steps aside and asks her supporters to make
the common campaign work.

Razem activists gain a candidate with the resources of the wider Left. New
Left's regional barons and Biedroń's progressive network see their announced
nominee displaced by negotiation. The posters carry one face; behind them, the
apparatus remembers who was asked to surrender.

- @poland_event_queue: Put Zandberg's common mandate on the events desk

@christmas_eve
# prose-audit: Grade B — A compact delivery scene names the labour sponsor and affected workers, distinguishes government authorship from opposition pressure, and retains the compromise after both exits.
title: A free Christmas Eve
subtitle: A visible workers' gain with a retail compromise attached
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-chamber.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 15
order: 30
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 12 and government_party != "pis" and caretaker_government = 0
on-arrival: government_delivery += 3; labor_credibility += 3; household_security += 2; news_headline = "Christmas Eve becomes a statutory day off from 2025"

= December 2024 — Claim the day or explain the Sundays

Parliament makes Christmas Eve a statutory day off from 2025 and pays for the
political agreement with additional trading Sundays in December. **Agnieszka
Dziemianowicz-Bąk**, Lewica's leading voice on labour policy, stands beside
retail workers who will gain the holiday. Shop owners and their employees are
already counting the busier Sundays which precede it.

[? if left_in_government = 1: Because Lewica helped govern the bill into law,
we can claim delivery—but we also own the compromise that made a majority.?]
[? if left_in_government = 0: Lewica can claim that years of labour pressure
moved the government, but not that an opposition party administered the
change. The cabinet which passed it will demand its share of the photograph.?]

The protection is real and so is its retail price. The only question left is
which half of the bargain we put in the headline.

- @eve_victory
- @eve_compromise

@eve_victory
title: Celebrate the paid day off as a Left labour victory
subtitle: Put the worker's holiday first and leave coalition partners to explain the concessions.
on-arrival: workers_support += 4; left_poll_momentum += 0.2; media_capacity += 2; ko_relation -= 1; news_headline = "The Left puts a labour label on Christmas Eve"

Dziemianowicz-Bąk meets retail workers finishing one of the last compulsory
Christmas Eve shifts and names the day off as a victory won by labour politics.
[? if left_in_government = 1: Our ministers put Lewica's signature above the
coalition logo; KO accepts the law and resents being edited out of its passage.?]
[? if left_in_government = 0: We claim the pressure that made refusal costly,
while the governing parties remind every camera that their votes enacted it.?]

The simpler story travels. The additional trading Sundays remain in the law,
waiting for unions and exhausted December staff to complicate the celebration.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the Christmas Eve victory on the events desk

@eve_compromise
title: Defend the full compromise, including extra trading Sundays
subtitle: Own the majority that passed the holiday and answer workers asked to cover its price.
on-arrival: public_trust -= 2; left_poll -= 0.2; left_poll_momentum -= 0.15; workers_support -= 2; labor_credibility -= 2; psl_relation += 2; ko_relation += 2; labor_dissent += 4; razem_dissent += 3; progressives_dissent += 2; news_headline = "The coalition owns both the day off and its retail price"

Lewica presents the law as it is: one guaranteed family day in exchange for a
December calendar with more Sunday opening. Employers and coalition partners
hear a party capable of admitting how legislation is assembled. Retail unions
hear their supposed champion defending extra Sunday shifts that still land on
cashiers, warehouse crews and transport staff.

[? if left_in_government = 1: The coalition owns a durable settlement and our
ministers own its least popular clause.?] [? if left_in_government = 0: From
opposition, we defend the government's compromise as necessary and make its
authors easier partners—while weakening our claim to have offered workers a
clearer alternative.?]

The holiday enters the calendar with no false promise that the concession
vanished after the vote. Every December rota will now remind voters who asked
them to applaud the headline and absorb the schedule.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the complete retail bargain on the events desk


@romanowski_hungary_2024
# prose-audit: Grade C — The flight, the Hungarian asylum and the connection to Ziobro's circle are properly staged, but the diplomatic response options still resolve faster than the real chain would.
title: Romanowski receives Hungarian asylum
subtitle: A suspect in the Justice Fund case leaves for Budapest
face-image: img/poland/events/viktor-orban-2022.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 27
order: 15
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 12 and romanowski_case_stage = 1 and romanowski_hungary_2024_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.romanowski_hungary_2024_done = 1;
Q.romanowski_case_stage = 2;
Q.hungary_relation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.hungary_relation) || 45) - 20
);
Q.justice_fund_salience =
    (Number(Q.justice_fund_salience) || 0) + 10;
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 3
);
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += -7;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 9;
Q.news_headline =
    "Hungary grants asylum to a Polish deputy wanted in the Justice Fund case";
!}

= December 2024 — Asylum inside the Union

Romanowski does not attend the court. He is in Budapest, and Hungary grants
him asylum on the grounds that he cannot expect a fair trial in Poland. One EU
member state has formally declared another's courts unsafe, over a case about
a domestic compensation fund.

For the camp around **Zbigniew Ziobro** this is a demonstration rather than an
escape: the argument that the Polish justice system is being used politically
now has a foreign government's signature on it. For everyone prosecuting the
fund, an entire branch of the case has moved outside Polish jurisdiction.

[? if ziobro_whereabouts_stage >= 2: Ziobro's own whereabouts have already
been a running national argument, and Budapest has now provided the template
for how that argument ends.?]
[? if romanowski_response = "Fund audit" or romanowski_response = "Fund publication": The
statutory audit of the fund continues regardless of where the defendant is
sitting, which is the one part of this that a flight cannot reach.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: Our foreign ministry has to decide how much of
the Union's patience to spend on one deputy.?][? if left_in_government = 0:
From opposition we can define what the response should have been, which is
easier and cheaper than producing one.?]

- @romanowski_hungary_legal
- @romanowski_hungary_diplomatic
- @romanowski_hungary_domestic

@romanowski_hungary_legal
title: Pursue it as a European legal question, not a quarrel with Budapest
subtitle: Slow, correct and undramatic; it keeps the case alive without letting Orbán choose the battlefield.
on-arrival: eu_relations += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 4; institutional_trust += 4; justice_fund_salience += 4; public_trust += 2; hungary_relation += 3; news_headline = "Warsaw takes the asylum decision to the European legal institutions"

The response is filed rather than shouted: mutual recognition of judicial
decisions is a treaty obligation, and a member state declaring another's
courts unsafe is a matter for the Union's own institutions. The paperwork is
dull and the case remains open.

It denies Budapest the confrontation it would enjoy and denies our own public
the satisfaction it would like. Both of those are the price of a route that
might actually return a defendant to a courtroom.

- @poland_event_queue: File the European legal response

@romanowski_hungary_diplomatic
title: Make it a public rupture with the Hungarian government
subtitle: Strong, popular and it converts a criminal case into a bilateral quarrel Orbán can win at home.
on-arrival: hungary_relation -= 15; eu_relations += 2; public_trust += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; pis_relation -= 6; justice_fund_salience -= 3; news_headline = "The asylum decision becomes an open quarrel between Warsaw and Budapest"

The ambassador is summoned, the language is undiplomatic and correct, and the
Polish public overwhelmingly agrees. Hungarian state media receives a week of
material about Polish persecution, which is precisely what it wanted.

The fund, the grants and the refused victim organisations disappear from
domestic coverage for the duration. The quarrel outlasts them.

- @poland_event_queue: Summon the ambassador

@romanowski_hungary_domestic
title: Keep the case domestic and legislate against absent defendants
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Ensures flight stops working, at the risk of writing procedure around one man.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No legislative capacity is free to draft an absent-defendant procedure.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; prosecution_command_clarity += 6; judicial_legitimacy += 2; institutional_trust += 3; administrative_reform_pressure += 3; public_trust += 2; constitutional_restraint -= 2; news_headline = "A procedure is written for defendants who leave the jurisdiction"

We write the rule that should already exist: what happens to proceedings, to a
parliamentary mandate and to public funds when a defendant leaves and does not
return. It applies generally, and it makes the next flight considerably less
attractive.

Lawyers point out, correctly, that legislation written with one face in mind
tends to fit that face and no other. We take the point and pass it anyway,
because the alternative is discovering the gap again with the next suspect.

- @poland_event_queue: Table the absent-defendant procedure

@pis_funding_chamber_2024
# prose-audit: Grade C — The recursive legitimacy trap is set out precisely and the three answers are genuinely different; the chamber's judges are named as a category rather than as people.
title: The appeal goes to a chamber the government calls unlawful
subtitle: A party finance ruling depends on judges whose legitimacy the coalition disputes
face-image: img/poland/events/supreme-court.webp
new-page: true
